From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:06:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable CPU cluster performance
 controllers

Enable the E and P cluster performance controllers on the 14-inch
MacBook Pro (M4, 2024).

No thermal owner exists for this board yet, so the T8132 cpufreq
driver keeps both clusters at or below P-state 4 (E cluster up to
1860 MHz, P cluster up to 1800 MHz). This still gives the kernel
control over the cluster frequencies instead of leaving them wherever
the boot firmware put them, and lets both clusters clock down when
idle. Releasing the full range needs a J604 thermal owner and is left
for a later change.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index d66c0b5840..f7ad4f2527 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -414,6 +414,19 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * CPU DVFS. Without a board thermal owner the T8132 cpufreq driver keeps both
+ * clusters at or below P-state 4 (E 1860 MHz, P 1800 MHz).
+ */
+&cpufreq_e {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&cpufreq_p {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 #include "t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi"
 
 /*
